1.1 In this step, the dataset is loaded, its structure is examined, and the text data (abstracts) is cleaned by removing noise such HTML elements, special characters, numerals, stop words, and applying lemmatization and lowercasing.

1.2 Column Identification and Feature Engineering: 
In this step we separate the pertinent text column (Cleaned_Abstract) and use TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency) vectorization to convert unstructured text into numerical feature representations that capture contextual relevance in order to enable semantic categorization of research papers.

